From: Shadow-MSM contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: borrow init page table for resident diagnostics

The initialized ARMPRG diagnostic runtime calls a polling USB transport whose
private MMIO and work-buffer mappings live in the early identity map.  Copying
only the runtime's 0x00800000 PGD entry into PID 1 preserves its instructions
and data but not every mapping reached through the initialized USB function
table.

Route C diagnostics through the board driver.  Its implementation saves the
active ARM926 TTBR, temporarily installs init_mm's already-validated page
table, emits one frame, and restores the process TTBR with IRQs masked.  This
keeps the firmware device map private to the tiny privileged trace window
instead of copying it into every userspace page table.

The helper is diagnostic-only and specific to CONFIG_SHADOW_MSM_EARLY_TRACE.

diff --git a/include/linux/shadow_msm_trace.h b/include/linux/shadow_msm_trace.h
index 28f9efc..8f61098 100644
--- a/include/linux/shadow_msm_trace.h
+++ b/include/linux/shadow_msm_trace.h
@@ -4,12 +4,11 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SHADOW_MSM_EARLY_TRACE
 void shadow_msm_watchdog_service(void);
+void shadow_msm_diag_emit(const char *message);
 
 static inline void shadow_msm_diag_trace(const char *message)
 {
-	shadow_msm_watchdog_service();
-	((void (*)(const char *))0x00816cf4UL)(message);
-	shadow_msm_watchdog_service();
+	shadow_msm_diag_emit(message);
 }
 
 static inline void shadow_msm_diag_hex(const char *prefix,
